<Styles xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml">
    <!-- ═══ Personalize → Text (RemEx-jt6w5) ═══

         Every type-scale member RemEx uses is re-declared here with the SAME KEY as Material's,
         BasedOn Material's empty base theme (MaterialTextBlock), with FontSize/FontWeight/Effect
         bound to Typo.* DynamicResources that TypographyService publishes. Use sites keep
         Theme="{StaticResource CaptionTextBlock}" — nothing at the hundreds of sites changes, and
         the vocabulary TypographyVocabularyTests enforces does not grow.

         Material 3.19.0's members are each MaterialTextBlock + one FontSize + one FontWeight
         setter (Material.Styles/Resources/Themes/TextBlock.axaml), so restating both here loses
         nothing. If a later Material version adds setters to a member, add them here too.

         WHY THIS IS A StyleInclude AFTER MaterialTheme, NOT A ResourceInclude: App.axaml parses
         Application.Resources before Application.Styles, and a ResourceInclude loads when merged,
         so its StaticResources would run before Material existed. Later Styles are searched first
         by Styles.TryGetResource, which is what lets these keys shadow Material's.

         NO DEFAULT VALUES HERE. TypographyService populates every Typo.* key in its constructor
         and ThemeService merges that dictionary before any window exists; a copy of the table in
         XAML would be the second copy that drifts. No inline FontSize="N" either — the ratchet
         in TypographyVocabularyTests only goes down. -->
    <Styles.Resources>
        <ResourceDictionary>

            <!-- Untagged text: EFFECT ONLY on the default TextBlock theme. A FontSize or FontWeight
                 setter here would outrank INHERITANCE and force a fixed value onto every
                 ContentPresenter TextBlock inside a Button, stripping the Medium/SemiBold Material
                 and RemEx's own button classes give button labels — untagged SIZE follows Body
                 through the MaterialDesignFontSize own key (App.axaml). Untagged BOLD's mechanism is
                 the Window style below, not this ControlTheme — see its comment for why (RemEx-jt6w5.11,
                 two abandoned attempts before it). -->
            <ControlTheme x:Key="{x:Type TextBlock}" TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource MaterialTextBlock}">
                <Setter Property="Effect" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Body.Effect}"/>
            </ControlTheme>

            <!-- Untagged BOLD (RemEx-jt6w5.11). THE MECHANISM, after two abandoned attempts:
                 THE ORIGINAL MECHANISM (shipped, then reverted): a runtime Avalonia.Styling.Style
                 attached/detached on Application.Styles only while Body bold was on. That mutation
                 of the live Styles collection broke UI Automation's FindAll on the shell root until
                 restart — confirmed against the real Windows UIA stack.
                 ATTEMPT 1 (never shipped): a FontWeight Setter on the default {x:Type TextBlock}
                 ControlTheme above, bound to this same DynamicResource, toggling the resource
                 between FontWeight.Bold and AvaloniaProperty.UnsetValue. Measured
                 (ShellTypographyBoldAutomationTests, GetDiagnostic) that the Unset value does NOT
                 make a ControlTheme setter a no-op: it registers a real Style-priority value frame
                 that resolves to the property's own default (Regular), and that frame outranked a
                 Button's own Style-priority FontWeight setter for its content TextBlock —
                 ConnectionStatusButton's StatusText (declared SemiBold via its own .secondary class)
                 measured Value=Normal, Priority=Style at BASELINE (Body bold OFF): a forced-Regular
                 regression.
                 ATTEMPT 2 (never shipped): TypographyService pushed the inherited weight directly
                 onto each already-open top-level window's root (IClassicDesktopStyleApplicationLifetime.Windows)
                 at Apply time. Measured broken for a different reason: both startup Apply calls
                 (App.axaml.cs's ApplyThemeBeforeWindowShown and the DashboardLayoutService.LoadAsync
                 path) run before MainWindow exists, so a persisted BodyBold=true opened the shell
                 Regular at cold start until the next settings change — and the same gap applied to
                 every on-demand window (TrayFlyoutWindow, PairingDialog, CommandPaletteWindow, etc.)
                 created after the last Apply.
                 THE MECHANISM: a STATIC Style, present from the moment Typography.axaml loads,
                 selecting every Window and setting the INHERITED attached property
                 TextElement.FontWeight (exposed in XAML as "TextBlock.FontWeight" — Avalonia
                 resolves attached-property Setters by the {Name}Property static field, which
                 TextBlock itself also exposes) to a DynamicResource this section keeps ALWAYS
                 PRESENT — FontWeight.Bold when Body bold is on, FontWeight.Normal (an explicit,
                 ordinary value, not AvaloniaProperty.UnsetValue) when off. A Window's own template
                 has no FontWeight setter of its own to conflict with this Style priority, so every
                 window gets the value from the moment it is constructed — cold start and every
                 on-demand window included, no per-window push required. Explicit Normal when off is
                 exactly what descendants would inherit if nothing were set at all, so it is harmless,
                 and it sidesteps the UnsetValue trap Attempt 1 hit. Children still behave correctly:
                 untagged text with no nearer ancestor inherits this value from the Window; Material
                 buttons and RemEx's own button classes (.secondary etc.) set FontWeight on
                 themselves at Style priority, a nearer ancestor, so their labels are never disturbed;
                 themed members and the .page-title/.card-title classes carry their own setters. A
                 Style (not a resource-keyed ControlTheme) can't live inside this ResourceDictionary,
                 so it is declared below, after Styles.Resources closes, as a direct child of
                 <Styles> alongside this StyleInclude's own root. -->

            <!-- ── Headers ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <ControlTheme x:Key="Headline5TextBlock" TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource MaterialTextBlock}">
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Headline5.FontSize}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Headline5.FontWeight}"/>
                <Setter Property="Effect" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Headers.Effect}"/>
            </ControlTheme>
            <ControlTheme x:Key="Headline6TextBlock" TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource MaterialTextBlock}">
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Headline6.FontSize}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Headline6.FontWeight}"/>
                <Setter Property="Effect" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Headers.Effect}"/>
            </ControlTheme>
            <ControlTheme x:Key="Subtitle1TextBlock" TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource MaterialTextBlock}">
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Subtitle1.FontSize}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Subtitle1.FontWeight}"/>
                <Setter Property="Effect" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Headers.Effect}"/>
            </ControlTheme>

            <!-- ── Body ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <ControlTheme x:Key="Body2TextBlock" TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource MaterialTextBlock}">
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Body2.FontSize}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Body2.FontWeight}"/>
                <Setter Property="Effect" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Body.Effect}"/>
            </ControlTheme>

            <!-- ── Small text ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── -->
            <ControlTheme x:Key="CaptionTextBlock" TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource MaterialTextBlock}">
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Caption.FontSize}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Caption.FontWeight}"/>
                <Setter Property="Effect" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Small.Effect}"/>
            </ControlTheme>
            <ControlTheme x:Key="OverlineTextBlock" TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource MaterialTextBlock}">
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Overline.FontSize}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Overline.FontWeight}"/>
                <Setter Property="Effect" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Small.Effect}"/>
            </ControlTheme>

            <!-- ── Sensor text ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
                 Applied by the sensor-card templates (CanvasView, HomeView pinned tiles, the tray
                 flyout strip) to the card TITLE and the dual-metric METRIC NAMES. Never the value
                 plate: that keeps Headline6TextBlock / Body1TextBlock and is out of scope. -->
            <ControlTheme x:Key="SensorTitleTextBlock" TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource MaterialTextBlock}">
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.SensorTitle.FontSize}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.SensorTitle.FontWeight}"/>
                <Setter Property="Effect" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Sensor.Effect}"/>
            </ControlTheme>
            <ControlTheme x:Key="SensorMetricNameTextBlock" TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource MaterialTextBlock}">
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.SensorMetricName.FontSize}"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.SensorMetricName.FontWeight}"/>
                <Setter Property="Effect" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.Sensor.Effect}"/>
            </ControlTheme>

        </ResourceDictionary>
    </Styles.Resources>

    <!-- Untagged BOLD's actual Setter (see the comment above, in Styles.Resources, for the full
         RemEx-jt6w5.11 history) — a Style, not a resource, so it lives here rather than inside
         Styles.Resources' ResourceDictionary. Selects every Window and sets the INHERITED attached
         property TextElement.FontWeight (exposed in XAML as "TextBlock.FontWeight") to a
         DynamicResource TypographyService keeps ALWAYS PRESENT: FontWeight.Bold when Body bold is
         on, FontWeight.Normal (an explicit ordinary value, not AvaloniaProperty.UnsetValue) when
         off. Present from the moment this file loads, so every window — cold start's MainWindow
         included, and every on-demand window (TrayFlyoutWindow, PairingDialog,
         CommandPaletteWindow, etc.) — gets the current value from construction, no per-window push
         required. -->
    <Style Selector="Window">
        <Setter Property="TextBlock.FontWeight" Value="{DynamicResource Typo.UntaggedBold.FontWeight}"/>
    </Style>
</Styles>
